@startuml
title Valetax Support Ticket Co-Pilot - Processing Sequence
actor Agent
boundary CLI
control Orchestrator
control "Pre-policy Gate" as Pre
control Classifier
control Retriever
control "Evidence Validator" as Evidence
control Provider
control "Post-policy Gate" as Post
control Router

Agent -> CLI : submit ticket
CLI -> Orchestrator : validate and process
Orchestrator -> Pre : input + ticket text

alt invalid input, unsupported language, injection, or protected intent
  Pre --> Orchestrator : safe result + reason
  Orchestrator -> Router : require human review
else eligible support request
  Pre --> Orchestrator : allowed
  Orchestrator -> Classifier : classify fields
  Classifier -> Provider : structured classification
  Provider --> Classifier : labels / typed failure
  Classifier --> Orchestrator : classifications
  Orchestrator -> Retriever : retrieve allowlisted sections
  Retriever --> Orchestrator : passages + provenance / failure

  alt missing, contradictory, or failed evidence
    Orchestrator -> Router : abstain + reason
  else sufficient evidence
    Orchestrator -> Evidence : validate evidence coverage
    Evidence --> Orchestrator : accepted passages
    Orchestrator -> Provider : draft only from evidence
    Provider --> Orchestrator : draft candidate / typed failure
    Orchestrator -> Post : validate claims, citations, and policy

    alt supported and safe
      Post --> Orchestrator : validated draft
      Orchestrator -> Router : agent review decision
    else unsafe or unsupported output
      Post --> Orchestrator : reject + reason
      Orchestrator -> Router : abstain and escalate
    end
  end
end

Router --> Orchestrator : route decision
Orchestrator --> CLI : validated structured JSON
CLI --> Agent : draft, abstention, evidence, and reasons

note over CLI,Agent
The co-pilot never sends directly to a customer.
end note
@enduml
